 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Honestly, the simple ones work best. A clean box or small container that opens upwards is easy to spot and easy for people to avoid. Keep it as close as you can without being right next to it. A clean box three or four feet away is much harder to spot. Make a plan together as a group. Often just talking about it makes the bears go away. If the bear is curious but doesn't eat anything, leave the area and call it day. If the bear is hungry and takes a snack, call a keeper. You've got this. Bears are fascinating animals, and the more you learn about them, the easier they become.",
